  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Other than $\\mathrm{S}$, seven letters $\\mathrm{M}, \\mathrm{I}, \\mathrm{I}, \\mathrm{I}, \\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{I}$ can be arranged in $\\frac{7 !}{2 ! 4 !}=7.5 .3$.\nNow four $\\mathrm{S}$ can be placed in 8 spaces in ${ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_4$ ways.\nDesired number of ways $=7.5 \\cdot 3 \\cdot{ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_4=7 \\cdot{ }^6 \\mathrm{C}_4 \\cdot{ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_4$",
    "image": null
  },
